<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Compose draws everything; this only needs to exist and stay out of the
      way. No AppCompat dependency, so the platform Material theme is fine, and
      it stays `Light` because `Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight` arrived in API 29
      and this app runs from 26.

      What matters here is windowBackground. The window is what shows through
      any frame the composition does not fully cover, and a crossfade between
      two screens is exactly that — so `@android:color/white` meant a white
      flash on every navigation, in dark mode too. The colour is `-night`
      qualified instead, which needs no theme support at all.

      That qualifier follows the *system* setting rather than the app's own
      toggle, which it has no way to know about. It only decides the frame
      before Compose draws; from there the Surface under the graph covers it.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.GisWrap" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/window_background</item>
    </style>
</resources>
